From 58d40c96e0e61f864bcd4181ba374910ae7cd098 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Arthur Souza Rodrigues <arthursrodrigues@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 26 Sep 2026 21:11:18 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 3/5] feat(python): Document facade, edit plans, PNG/render,
 module CLI with binary parity

- Applies the proposed 0002 facade (immutable Document, CompareOptions,
  PdfOptions, typed Revision) and extends it: sha256(), inspect() ->
  Snapshot, markdown(), edit(plan) -> EditResult, preview(plan),
  to_png(dpi), render(pdf, png_dpi) -> Rendered; EditPlan builder that
  serializes the engine's wire schema; EditPlanError carries code,
  operation and per-operation outcomes; capabilities().
- Native exports: docx_to_png, render, source_sha256, inspect_json,
  markdown, edit_json, preview_json, report_jsonl, capabilities_json; all
  compute detached from the interpreter; structured results cross as the
  engine's own JSON.
- python -m jubarte_redlines: inspect, text, edit, convert, compare,
  revisions, accept, reject, capabilities with the binary's flags, output
  names and exit codes (3 = plan refused).
- 48 tests against the rebuilt binding: 98% lines, 160/166 branches.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01XSguJyaPYNYbKNxFYkEmvV
